---
source: crates/pixi_manifest/src/manifests/workspace.rs
expression: "expect_parse_warnings(r#\"\n[workspace]\nname = \"foo\"\nchannels = []\nplatforms = []\nexclude-newer = \"7d\"\n\n[exclude-newer]\npolars = \"0d\"\nopenssl = \"2025-01-01\"\n\n[pypi-exclude-newer]\nboltons = \"0d\"\n\"#)"
---
  ⚠ the top-level `[exclude-newer]` table of per-package cutoffs is deprecated in favor of the `exemptions` of `[workspace.exclude-newer]`
    ╭─[pixi.toml:8:1]
  7 │
  8 │ ╭─▶ [exclude-newer]
  9 │ │   polars = "0d"
 10 │ ├─▶ openssl = "2025-01-01"
    · ╰──── replace this with `[workspace.exclude-newer.exemptions]`
 11 │
    ╰────
  help: move the entries with a zero cutoff to the `exemptions` of `[workspace.exclude-newer]` instead, e.g. replace the current `exclude-newer` of `[workspace]` with

        [workspace.exclude-newer]
        cutoff = "7days"
        exemptions = { polars = "*" }

        An exemption allows the matching releases regardless of their upload time. Narrow `"*"` down to the releases you vetted, e.g. `"1.2.3"`.

        per-package cutoffs other than a zero cutoff have no replacement, the cutoffs of `openssl` will stop working when the table is removed in a future release

  ⚠ the top-level `[pypi-exclude-newer]` table of per-package cutoffs is deprecated in favor of the `exemptions` of `[workspace.pypi-exclude-newer]`
    ╭─[pixi.toml:12:1]
 11 │
 12 │ ╭─▶ [pypi-exclude-newer]
 13 │ ├─▶ boltons = "0d"
    · ╰──── replace this with `[workspace.pypi-exclude-newer.exemptions]`
    ╰────
  help: move the entries to the `exemptions` of `[workspace.pypi-exclude-newer]` instead, e.g. replace the current `pypi-exclude-newer` of `[workspace]` with

        [workspace.pypi-exclude-newer]
        exemptions = { boltons = "*" }

        An exemption allows every release of the package regardless of its upload time.
